  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe setup orientation UI is two dropdowns, one section everywhere\n(#771, stacked on #770):\n\n- **Plane orientation** - Axes (#769, the default), Points (#555),\n  Face (#330), Manual (the preset/angles picker), and the new\n  **Cylinder angle**: one pick on a bore's or cylinder's curved wall\n  names its axis from the wall's own facet normals (any two\n  non-parallel wall normals cross exactly along it; every other\n  normal is verified - a mixed patch is refused by name, never\n  misread). The axis lands on a chosen world axis (+X/+Y/+Z), turned\n  by an angle about it, the part turning about its bounds centre.\n- **Orientation point** - the parts' bounds or the setup's stock\n  (corner or centre), or a picked vertex. The WCS's rotation is kept:\n  the frame comes from the plane side; each setup places its own WCS\n  (`SetWcsOrigin::for_setup`), never the active one's.\n- The section is ONE component (`setup_orient_pick::section`) mounted\n  on the Setups overview AND each setup's Settings page - same\n  dropdowns, same options, same look (the user's law). The old rows\n  keep their own entry points and draw verbatim as the expanded\n  content.\n\n## How tested\n\n- New `crates/app/tests/orient_dropdowns.rs` (9 tests): a tilted\n  cylinder's wall lands its axis on Z (end to end: every wall normal\n  in the setup frame perpendicular to it); a 90-degree angle swings\n  the wall about the landed axis and keeps the axis put; X and Y\n  landings; a flat face, an edge and a NaN angle refused by name; the\n  model box corner/centre places the setup's WCS (undo removes it);\n  the stock box corner/centre; placing the origin keeps a pre-set\n  rotation; each setup places its own WCS (Setup1 untouched); the\n  missing model and stock refused by name.\n- UI: the structural twin `setup_page_alignment_rows_structure`\n  rewritten for the dropdowns (two combos, axes rows expanded by\n  default, the other methods behind their entries, the origin side's\n  box reading); `setup_picks_disarm` switches the dropdown before\n  clicking the plane/points rows (switch_plane_method) - all 8 green\n  again. Battery green: ui 37 (setup_axis, structural, disarm,\n  one_pick_rule, plane, points, align), orient_dropdowns 9,\n  align_axes 9, axis_align 10, plane_align 9, points_align 8,\n  turn_pivot 5; clippy clean on camcraft-app and camcraft-ui.\n\n## What was not exercised\n\n- The dropdown's method selection persists per egui session only (a\n  page reopen resets to the defaults); the picks themselves follow\n  the #664 pause law as before.\n- The vertex origin pick needs a model with vertices in the viewport -\n  pinned at the app layer (`place_setup_origin`'s Vertex arm reads\n  the same `vertex` the 3-2-1 flow uses); the full viewport click\n  path is covered by the disarm suites' click plumbing, not a new\n  end-to-end vertex case.\n\nChangelog: feat(ui): two orientation dropdowns on the Setups pages - plane method (axes/points/face/manual/cylinder angle) and origin point (model box/stock box/vertex), one section everywhere (#771, PR)\n\nFixes #771\n",
